<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- FORSAKEN_CRAGS_PREDATORS_BUILD_1 - wires RSW_Cindermare and RSW_Skarnix
     into the Forsaken Crags' wildAnimals dictionary. Without this the two
     PawnKindDefs built earlier for this item would never spawn wild anywhere
     - "both creatures spawn on the Forsaken Crags" is a real criterion, not
     flavor text, and nothing in the ThingDef/PawnKindDef pair links them to
     a biome by itself.

     🔴 RETARGETED 2026-09-25 (FORSAKENCRAGS_RM_MOD_BUILD_1): this patch
     originally targeted the DONOR AB_RockyCrags (Alpha Biomes' own "Forsaken
     Crags"), authored 2026-09-02, before RUT_ForsakenCrags existed
     (2026-09-09) and before the RimMandrake split (2026-09-25) — so it never
     once wired these two predators into either def our campaign actually
     uses. Per biome_mod_architecture.md §5 step 2, every RSW_/SW_ creature
     stays out of the RM_ BiomeDef itself and rides here instead, now
     targeting RM_ForsakenCrags (this campaign's live def is the frozen
     RUT_ForsakenCrags twin, which carries the world only until the terminal
     paint — Star Wars content is never added to a RUT_ twin, so RM_
     ForsakenCrags is correct even though the world does not carry it yet).

     Guarded with PatchOperationConditional on the biome's own wildAnimals
     node rather than a hard modDependency: if mandrake.rm.forsakencrags
     isn't loaded the condition is false and this whole op is a silent no-op
     (CLAUDE.md's "PatchOperationConditional/FindMod return true on no match"
     trap does not bite here because we gate on the TARGET NODE existing, not
     on the mod's presence) - correct, because this mod's other content
     (Karrask livestock) does not need the Forsaken Crags mod at all.

     Commonalities picked relative to the biome's existing background vermin
     (AA_DuskRat 1.5) - both new predators are rarer than the biome's
     background vermin, Skarnix (cat-large stalker) somewhat more common than
     Cindermare (larger, more dangerous solitary threat). Unchanged from the
     original ruling. -->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_ForsakenCrags"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_ForsakenCrags"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_Cindermare>0.04</RSW_Cindermare>
        <RSW_Skarnix>0.09</RSW_Skarnix>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
